IMPORT prelude

-- Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth) -- Schedule 2, the Australian Consumer Law, as the consumer meets it: who acquires
-- goods or services "as a consumer" (Sch 2 s 3, with the $100,000 prescribed by reg 77A of the Competition and Consumer
-- Regulations 2010); the consumer guarantees for goods and which of them the supplier answers for (ss 54-59, 259(1)); major
-- and minor failures and the remedies against the supplier, including who chooses the remedy and what happens on rejection
-- (ss 259-263); terms that try to exclude the guarantees (ss 64, 64A); unfair terms in consumer and small business contracts
-- (ss 23, 24, 26, 27); unsolicited consumer agreements -- the door-knock and the cold call, permitted hours, the dealer leaving
-- on request, the termination ("cooling-off") period, payment and supply during it (ss 69, 73, 75, 82, 85(3), 86, with regs
-- 81 and 95); misleading or deceptive conduct (s 18); harassment and coercion (s 50); the Schedule's reach as a law of the
-- Commonwealth (ss 131, 131A); and, for Daniel's acquisition of Formly only, when an acquisition must be notified to the ACCC
-- under Part IVA (ss 51ABB, 51ABD, 51ABE(2), 51ABJ, 51ABO, 51ABP, 51ABS(1), 51ABT(1), 51ABV(1)).
--
-- SEAT: the consumer -- the person who buys goods or services, or is door-knocked or called, and the small business that
-- contracts on standard terms (Daniel's company Jarrah, as customer and as trader) -- "What guarantees and protections do I
-- have, and what may not be done to me?". Every decision is phrased as that person asks it. Where the Act addresses the
-- supplier or dealer ("the supplier must", "a dealer must not") it is encoded as what may be done to the consumer, what the
-- consumer must be given, and when. Where the Act hands a judgment to a court (acceptable quality, major failure, unfair,
-- misleading, undue harassment, the rejection period, "not fair or reasonable") it is asked as a fact. For Part IVA the seat
-- is Daniel as the acquirer: "Must I notify the ACCC?".
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 166, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 76, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00389, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00109.txt. The deposit's metadata warns that a version in
-- force from 16 September 2026 had no registered compilation when fetched, so amendments from that date may be missing.
-- Competition and Consumer Regulations 2010, Compilation No. 100, compilation date 1 September 2026 (includes amendments up
-- to F2026L01038), register id F2026C00856, as deposited at
-- ../../../competition-and-consumer-regulations-2010/registers/source-bundle/F1996B01420.txt -- regs 77A, 81, 95, 100 and the
-- endnote giving 1 July 2021 as the commencement of reg 77A.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Everything outside Schedule 2 except ss 131, 131A and the Part IVA provisions named above: Part IV (restrictive
-- trade practices), the rest of Part IVA (notification procedure, ACCC determinations, phase 2, public benefit, Tribunal
-- review), the industry codes, the access regimes, telecommunications and energy. In Schedule 2: the guarantees as to title
-- (ss 51-53) beyond their name; the services guarantees and remedies (ss 60-63, 267-270); the manufacturer's liability for
-- ss 54-59 (ss 271-274), which is where s 58 and s 59(1) are enforced; gift recipients (s 266); s 3(4)-(9) (how the price is
-- worked out for mixed supplies and credit: the price is an input); the s 25 examples of unfair terms; ss 28, 28A; the
-- unsolicited consumer agreement disclosure and document rules (ss 74, 76, 78-81: whether they were contravened is an input),
-- ss 83-84, 87-95 beyond reg 95, and the reg 88 and 89 emergency-repair and energy exclusions; the rest of Part 2-1 and Part
-- 3-1 (false representations, unsolicited supplies, pricing, lay-by); product safety; information standards; penalties,
-- injunctions, damages and enforcement (Chapters 4 and 5) except s 259; the ACCC/ASIC debt collection guideline (k064 names it;
-- it is not law); the ACL as a law of Western Australia (applied by the Fair Trading Act 2010 (WA), not deposited); the
-- Competition and Consumer (Notification of Acquisitions) Determination 2025, which sets the Part IVA thresholds and is NOT
-- deposited -- whether an acquisition meets a threshold is an INPUT. "Corporation", "financial services", "financial
-- products", "control" (Corporations Act s 50AA), "voting power" and "listed company" are borrowed terms, asked as facts.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers; clock times as hhmm on a 24-hour clock (5.30 pm is 1730).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Competition and Consumer Act 2010 -- the Australian Consumer Law from the consumer's seat`

§§ `ss 131, 131A -- does the Schedule reach my dealing as a law of the Commonwealth`

-- s 131(1): "Schedule 2 applies as a law of the Commonwealth to the conduct of corporations". (The extensions in ss 5, 6 and
-- 131(2) are not modelled.) s 131A(1): "Despite section 131, this Division does not apply ... to the supply, or possible
-- supply, of services that are financial services, or of financial products". (2)(a): Part 2-1 (s 18) does "not apply to
-- conduct engaged in in relation to financial services"; (2)(b): Part 2-3 (unfair terms) does not apply to contracts that are
-- financial products or for financial services. Gloss: "financial services" and "financial products" are ASIC Act and
-- Corporations Act terms, asked as a fact.
@export Does the Australian Consumer Law reach my dealing with this trader as a law of the Commonwealth (ss 131, 131A)?
GIVEN `the trader is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business you dealt with is a corporation (a company)
      `it concerns financial services or financial products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dealing is about financial services or a financial product, such as credit or insurance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the ACL reach my dealing as Commonwealth law` IF
    `the trader is a corporation` AND (NOT `it concerns financial services or financial products`)

§§ `Sch 2 s 3; Regulations reg 77A -- did I acquire it as a consumer`

-- s 3(1): "A person is taken to have acquired particular goods as a consumer if, and only if: (a) the amount paid or payable
-- for the goods ... did not exceed: (i) $40,000; or (ii) if a greater amount is prescribed for the purposes of this
-- paragraph--that greater amount; or (b) the goods were of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use
-- or consumption; or (c) the goods consisted of a vehicle or trailer acquired for use principally in the transport of goods on
-- public roads." Reg 77A: "For the purposes of paragraph 3(1)(a) of the Australian Consumer Law, the amount of $100,000 is
-- prescribed." The Regulations' endnotes give reg 77A's commencement as 1 July 2021 (Treasury Laws Amendment (Acquisition as
-- Consumer--Financial Thresholds) Regulations 2020, sch 1 items 3, 4), and reg 100 applies it to goods or services "acquired on
-- or after the commencement".
`the amount in s 3(1)(a)(i)` MEANS 40000
`the amount prescribed by reg 77A` MEANS 100000
`the day reg 77A commenced` MEANS 20210701

@export What is the most I can pay for goods or services and still acquire them as a consumer whatever their kind (Sch 2 s 3(1)(a); reg 77A)?
GIVEN `the date I acquired them` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you acquired the goods or services, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the consumer price limit on` IS
    IF `the date I acquired them` AT LEAST `the day reg 77A commenced`
    THEN `the amount prescribed by reg 77A`
    ELSE `the amount in s 3(1)(a)(i)`

-- s 3(2): "However, subsection (1) does not apply if the person acquired the goods ... (a) ... for the purpose of re-supply;
-- or (b) for the purpose of using them up or transforming them, in trade or commerce" in production, manufacture or repair.
-- s 3(3): services likewise by (a) the price test or (b) the personal kind, with no re-supply exception.
-- s 2: "goods includes ... (e) computer software". s 3(10): a person alleged to be a consumer "is presumed, unless the contrary
-- is established" to be one. The price under s 3(4)-(9) is an input.
DECLARE `My acquisition` HAS
    `goods rather than services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date acquired` IS A NUMBER
    `price paid or payable` IS A NUMBER
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a vehicle or trailer mainly for transporting goods on public roads` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired for re-supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired to use up or transform in production, manufacture or repair` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Did I acquire the goods or services as a consumer (Sch 2 s 3)?
GIVEN `what I acquired` IS A `My acquisition` @desc What you bought or acquired, when, for how much, and for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I acquire it as a consumer` IF
    IF `what I acquired`'s `goods rather than services`
    THEN     (    `what I acquired`'s `price paid or payable` AT MOST `What is the consumer price limit on` (`what I acquired`'s `date acquired`)
              OR  `what I acquired`'s `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption`
              OR  `what I acquired`'s `a vehicle or trailer mainly for transporting goods on public roads`)
         AND (NOT `what I acquired`'s `acquired for re-supply`)
         AND (NOT `what I acquired`'s `acquired to use up or transform in production, manufacture or repair`)
    ELSE     `what I acquired`'s `price paid or payable` AT MOST `What is the consumer price limit on` (`what I acquired`'s `date acquired`)
          OR `what I acquired`'s `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption`

§§ `Sch 2 ss 54-59 -- the guarantees I have for goods`

-- s 54(1): "If: (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and (b) the supply does not occur by way of
-- sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the goods are of acceptable quality." Sections 55, 56, 57, 58 and 59 open with
-- the same two conditions.
@export Do I have the guarantee that my goods are of acceptable quality (Sch 2 s 54(1))?
GIVEN `supplied in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a business sold or supplied the goods to you (not a private seller)
      `I acquired them as a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquired the goods as a consumer (Sch 2 s 3)
      `sold by auction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the goods at an auction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the guarantee of acceptable quality` IF
    `supplied in trade or commerce` AND `I acquired them as a consumer` AND (NOT `sold by auction`)

-- s 54(2): acceptable quality means as "(a) fit for all the purposes for which goods of that kind are commonly supplied; and
-- (b) acceptable in appearance and finish; and (c) free from defects; and (d) safe; and (e) durable; as a reasonable consumer
-- fully acquainted with the state and condition of the goods (including any hidden defects ...) would regard as acceptable",
-- having regard to the nature and price of the goods, packaging statements, representations and other circumstances (3).
-- (4): taken to be of acceptable quality if "the only reason or reasons why they are not ... were specifically drawn to the
-- consumer's attention before the consumer agreed to the supply" ((5): a transparent written notice displayed with them).
-- (6): they do not fail if "(a) the consumer ... causes them to become of unacceptable quality, or fails to take reasonable
-- steps to prevent them from becoming of unacceptable quality; AND (b) they are damaged by abnormal use" -- both limbs.
-- (7): nor if the consumer examined them and "the examination ought reasonably to have revealed" the problem.
DECLARE `State of my goods` HAS
    `a reasonable consumer would regard them as fit, finished, free from defects, safe and durable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only reasons were drawn to my attention before I agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I caused it or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damaged by abnormal use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my examination before buying ought to have revealed it` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Are my goods of acceptable quality (Sch 2 s 54(2)-(7))?
GIVEN `my goods` IS A `State of my goods` @desc The state of your goods, and how any fault came about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my goods of acceptable quality` IF
        `my goods`'s `a reasonable consumer would regard them as fit, finished, free from defects, safe and durable`
    OR  `my goods`'s `the only reasons were drawn to my attention before I agreed`
    OR  (`my goods`'s `I caused it or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent it` AND `my goods`'s `damaged by abnormal use`)
    OR  `my goods`'s `my examination before buying ought to have revealed it`

-- s 259(1): a consumer may take action against the supplier if "(b) a guarantee that applies to the supply under Subdivision A
-- of Division 1 of Part 3-2 (other than sections 58 and 59(1)) is not complied with". s 58 (repairs and spare parts) and
-- s 59(1) (the manufacturer's express warranty) are guarantees about what the MANUFACTURER will do; they are enforced against
-- the manufacturer (s 271), which is not encoded.
DECLARE Guarantee IS ONE OF
    `title, undisturbed possession and no undisclosed securities (ss 51-53)`
    `acceptable quality (s 54)`
    `fitness for a disclosed purpose (s 55)`
    `correspondence with description (s 56)`
    `correspondence with sample or demonstration model (s 57)`
    `repairs and spare parts (s 58)`
    `the manufacturer's express warranty (s 59(1))`
    `the supplier's express warranty (s 59(2))`

@export Can I take action against the supplier when this guarantee fails (Sch 2 s 259(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the guarantee` IS A Guarantee @desc Which consumer guarantee was not complied with
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I act against the supplier for this guarantee` IF
    CONSIDER `the guarantee`
    WHEN `repairs and spare parts (s 58)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the manufacturer's express warranty (s 59(1))` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Sch 2 ss 259-263 -- major and minor failures, and what I can do`

-- s 260(1): a failure is a major failure if "(a) the goods would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully
-- acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or (b) the goods depart in one or more significant respects" from
-- description or sample; "(c) the goods are substantially unfit for a purpose for which goods of the same kind are commonly
-- supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied ...; or (d) the goods are unfit for a disclosed
-- purpose ... and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied ...; or (e) the goods are not of acceptable
-- quality because they are unsafe." (2): also where it is one of "2 or more failures" and the goods "would not have been
-- acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of those failures, taken as a whole".
-- s 262(1): no rejection if "(a) the rejection period ... has ended; or (b) the goods have been lost, destroyed or disposed of
-- by the consumer; or (c) ... damaged after being delivered ... for reasons not related to their state or condition at the
-- time of supply; or (d) ... attached to, or incorporated in" other property and cannot be detached without damage. (2): the
-- rejection period is the time within which "it would be reasonable to expect the relevant failure ... to become apparent" --
-- a judgment, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My failure` HAS
    `a guarantee was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the guarantee` IS A Guarantee
    `a reasonable consumer would not have bought them knowing of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `departs significantly from the description or sample` IS A BOOLEAN
    `substantially unfit for a common purpose and not easily remedied in a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unfit for a disclosed purpose and not easily remedied in a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unsafe` IS A BOOLEAN
    `several failures taken together would have deterred a reasonable consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `can be remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I required a remedy and the supplier refused or failed within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rejection period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I lost, destroyed or disposed of them, they were damaged after delivery for other reasons, or they cannot be detached` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is the failure of my goods a major failure (Sch 2 s 260)?
GIVEN `the failure` IS A `My failure` @desc What went wrong with your goods
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a major failure` IF
        `the failure`'s `a reasonable consumer would not have bought them knowing of it`
    OR  `the failure`'s `departs significantly from the description or sample`
    OR  `the failure`'s `substantially unfit for a common purpose and not easily remedied in a reasonable time`
    OR  `the failure`'s `unfit for a disclosed purpose and not easily remedied in a reasonable time`
    OR  `the failure`'s `unsafe`
    OR  `the failure`'s `several failures taken together would have deterred a reasonable consumer`

@export Am I still entitled to reject the goods (Sch 2 s 262)?
GIVEN `the failure` IS A `My failure` @desc What went wrong with your goods, and what has happened to them since
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still entitled to reject` IF
        (NOT `the failure`'s `the rejection period has ended`)
    AND (NOT `the failure`'s `I lost, destroyed or disposed of them, they were damaged after delivery for other reasons, or they cannot be detached`)

-- s 259(2): "If the failure ... can be remedied and is not a major failure: (a) the consumer may require the supplier to remedy
-- the failure within a reasonable time; or (b) if ... the supplier refuses or fails to comply ... or fails to comply ... within
-- a reasonable time--the consumer may: (i) otherwise have the failure remedied and ... recover all reasonable costs ...; or (ii)
-- subject to section 262, notify the supplier that the consumer rejects the goods".
-- (3): "If the failure ... cannot be remedied or is a major failure, the consumer may: (a) subject to section 262, notify the
-- supplier that the consumer rejects the goods ...; or (b) ... recover compensation for any reduction in the value of the goods
-- below the price paid or payable".
-- s 261: when the consumer requires a remedy, "the supplier may comply ... (b) ... by repairing the goods; or (c) by replacing
-- the goods with goods of an identical type; or (d) by refunding" -- THE SUPPLIER picks. s 263(4): on rejection the supplier
-- must, "in accordance with an election made by the consumer", refund or replace -- THE CONSUMER picks.
-- s 259(7): action may be taken "whether or not the goods are in their original packaging".
DECLARE `What I can do` IS ONE OF
    `nothing against the supplier under s 259`
    `require the supplier to remedy it, and the supplier chooses repair, replacement or refund`
    `have it fixed elsewhere and recover the cost, or reject the goods`
    `have it fixed elsewhere and recover the cost; rejection is lost`
    `reject the goods and choose a refund or replacement, or claim the drop in value`
    `claim the drop in value; rejection is lost`

@export What can I do about the failure of my goods, and who chooses the remedy (Sch 2 ss 259, 261, 262, 263(4))?
GIVEN `the failure` IS A `My failure` @desc What went wrong with your goods, and what has happened since
GIVETH A `What I can do`
DECIDE `What can I do about my goods` IS
    IF (NOT `the failure`'s `a guarantee was not complied with`) OR (NOT `Can I act against the supplier for this guarantee` (`the failure`'s `the guarantee`))
    THEN `nothing against the supplier under s 259`
    ELSE IF `Is it a major failure` `the failure` OR (NOT `the failure`'s `can be remedied`)
         THEN IF `Am I still entitled to reject` `the failure`
              THEN `reject the goods and choose a refund or replacement, or claim the drop in value`
              ELSE `claim the drop in value; rejection is lost`
         ELSE IF `the failure`'s `I required a remedy and the supplier refused or failed within a reasonable time`
              THEN IF `Am I still entitled to reject` `the failure`
                   THEN `have it fixed elsewhere and recover the cost, or reject the goods`
                   ELSE `have it fixed elsewhere and recover the cost; rejection is lost`
              ELSE `require the supplier to remedy it, and the supplier chooses repair, replacement or refund`

-- s 263(4): "The supplier must, in accordance with an election made by the consumer: (a) refund: (i) any money paid by the
-- consumer for the goods; and (ii) an amount that is equal to the value of any other consideration ...; or (b) replace the
-- rejected goods with goods of the same type, and of similar value, if such goods are reasonably available to the supplier."
-- (5): "The supplier cannot satisfy subsection (4)(a) by permitting the consumer to acquire goods from the supplier" -- a store
-- credit is not a refund. The Act does not say what follows when the consumer elects a replacement and none is reasonably
-- available; that case is returned as such, not guessed.
DECLARE `My election` IS ONE OF
    `a refund`
    `a replacement`

DECLARE `What the supplier must give me` IS ONE OF
    `a refund of what I paid, not a store credit`
    `a replacement of the same type and similar value`
    `the Act does not say: I chose a replacement and none is reasonably available`

@export Having rejected the goods, what must the supplier give me (Sch 2 s 263(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my election` IS A `My election` @desc Whether you choose a refund or a replacement
      `a replacement is reasonably available to the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether goods of the same type and similar value are reasonably available to the supplier
GIVETH A `What the supplier must give me`
DECIDE `What must the supplier give me on rejection` IS
    CONSIDER `my election`
    WHEN `a refund` THEN `a refund of what I paid, not a store credit`
    WHEN `a replacement` THEN
        IF `a replacement is reasonably available to the supplier`
        THEN `a replacement of the same type and similar value`
        ELSE `the Act does not say: I chose a replacement and none is reasonably available`

-- s 263(2): "The consumer must return the goods to the supplier unless: (a) the goods have already been returned to, or
-- retrieved by, the supplier; or (b) the goods cannot be returned, removed or transported without significant cost to the
-- consumer because of: (i) the nature of the failure ...; or (ii) the size or height, or method of attachment, of the goods."
-- (3): in case (b) "the supplier must, within a reasonable time, collect the goods at the supplier's expense".
@export Having rejected the goods, must I return them myself (Sch 2 s 263(2), (3))?
GIVEN `already returned or retrieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supplier already has the goods back
      `returning them would cost me significantly because of the fault, their size or height, or how they are attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether returning the goods would cost you significantly because of the fault or their size, height or attachment (then the supplier must collect them)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I return the goods myself` IF
    (NOT `already returned or retrieved`) AND (NOT `returning them would cost me significantly because of the fault, their size or height, or how they are attached`)

-- s 259(4): "The consumer may, by action against the supplier, recover damages for any loss or damage suffered by the consumer
-- because of the failure ... if it was reasonably foreseeable that the consumer would suffer such loss or damage". (5): not if
-- the failure "occurred only because of a cause independent of human control that occurred after the goods left the control
-- of the supplier". (6): this is in addition to (2) and (3).
@export Can I also recover damages for my other loss from the supplier (Sch 2 s 259(4), (5))?
GIVEN `a guarantee was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guarantee the supplier answers for was not complied with
      `the loss was reasonably foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reasonably foreseeable that you would suffer this loss from such a failure
      `the failure was caused only by something independent of human control after the goods left the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure happened only because of something beyond human control after the goods left the supplier (for example lightning)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I recover damages for my loss` IF
        `a guarantee was not complied with`
    AND `the loss was reasonably foreseeable`
    AND (NOT `the failure was caused only by something independent of human control after the goods left the supplier`)

§§ `Sch 2 ss 64, 64A -- can a term take my guarantees away`

-- s 64(1): "A term of a contract ... is void to the extent that the term purports to exclude, restrict or modify, or has the
-- effect of excluding, restricting or modifying: (a) the application of all or any of the provisions of this Division; or (b)
-- the exercise of a right conferred by such a provision; or (c) any liability of a person for a failure to comply with a
-- guarantee". (2): only "if the term does so expressly or is inconsistent with the provision".
-- s 64A(1): for goods "other than goods of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption",
-- a term is not void "merely because the term limits the person's liability for failure to comply with a guarantee (other
-- than a guarantee under section 51, 52 or 53) to" replacement, repair, or the cost of either; (2): for such services, "to: (a)
-- the supplying of the services again; or (b) the payment of the cost of having the services supplied again." (3): s 64A does
-- not apply "if the person to whom the goods or services were supplied establishes that it is not fair or reasonable for the
-- person who supplied the goods or services to rely on that term". A cap at a sum of money -- the subscription fee -- is none
-- of the s 64A forms (an inference from the words; the life does not give the cap's wording).
DECLARE `The term` HAS
    `expressly or inconsistently excludes, restricts or modifies the guarantees or liability for them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supply is of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limits liability only to the s 64A remedies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it limits liability for the title guarantees in ss 51 to 53` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the customer establishes reliance on it is not fair or reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is this term void because it takes away the consumer guarantees (Sch 2 ss 64, 64A)?
GIVEN `the term` IS A `The term` @desc The contract term, what it does to the guarantees, and the kind of supply
      `the customer acquired as a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the customer acquired the goods or services as a consumer (Sch 2 s 3); only then do the guarantees exist
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the term void under s 64` IF
        `the customer acquired as a consumer`
    AND `the term`'s `expressly or inconsistently excludes, restricts or modifies the guarantees or liability for them`
    AND (NOT (    (NOT `the term`'s `the supply is of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use`)
              AND `the term`'s `limits liability only to the s 64A remedies`
              AND (NOT `the term`'s `it limits liability for the title guarantees in ss 51 to 53`)
              AND (NOT `the term`'s `the customer establishes reliance on it is not fair or reasonable`)))

§§ `Sch 2 ss 23, 24, 26, 27 -- unfair terms in consumer and small business contracts`

-- s 23(4): "A contract is a small business contract if: (a) the contract is for a supply of goods or services, or a sale or
-- grant of an interest in land; and (b) at least one party to the contract satisfies either or both of the following
-- conditions: (i) the party makes the contract in the course of carrying on a business and at a time when the party employs
-- fewer than 100 persons; (ii) the party's turnover ... for the party's last income year ... is less than $10,000,000."
-- (5): casuals count only if "regular and systematic"; part-timers as "an appropriate fraction of a full-time equivalent" --
-- the head count is an input. No limit on the contract's value appears.
DECLARE `Contracting party` HAS
    `contracts in the course of carrying on a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `persons employed, counted under s 23(5)` IS A NUMBER
    `turnover for its last income year` IS A NUMBER

`the small business head count` MEANS 100
`the small business turnover` MEANS 10000000

@export Is my contract a small business contract (Sch 2 s 23(4))?
GIVEN `my side` IS A `Contracting party` @desc Your business: whether you contract in the course of business, your head count and last year's turnover
      `the other side` IS A `Contracting party` @desc The other party, on the same facts
      `for a supply of goods, services or land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is for a supply of goods or services, or a sale or grant of an interest in land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract a small business contract` IF
        `for a supply of goods, services or land`
    AND (    (`my side`'s `contracts in the course of carrying on a business` AND `my side`'s `persons employed, counted under s 23(5)` LESS THAN `the small business head count`)
         OR  `my side`'s `turnover for its last income year` LESS THAN `the small business turnover`
         OR  (`the other side`'s `contracts in the course of carrying on a business` AND `the other side`'s `persons employed, counted under s 23(5)` LESS THAN `the small business head count`)
         OR  `the other side`'s `turnover for its last income year` LESS THAN `the small business turnover`)

-- s 23(3): "A consumer contract is a contract for: (a) a supply of goods or services; or (b) a sale or grant of an interest in
-- land; to an individual whose acquisition of the goods, services or interest is wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic
-- or household use or consumption."
@export Is my contract a consumer contract (Sch 2 s 23(3))?
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contract as an individual (not a company)
      `wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic or household use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquire the goods, services or land wholly or mainly for personal, domestic or household use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract a consumer contract` IF
    `I am an individual` AND `wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic or household use`

-- s 24(1): unfair if "(a) it would cause a significant imbalance in the parties' rights and obligations ...; and (b) it is not
-- reasonably necessary in order to protect the legitimate interests of the party who would be advantaged by the term; and (c)
-- it would cause detriment (whether financial or otherwise) to a party if it were to be applied or relied on." (4): limb (b)
-- "is presumed ... unless that party proves otherwise".
-- s 26(1): s 23 does not apply to a term to the extent it "(a) ... defines the main subject matter of the contract; or (b) ...
-- sets the upfront price payable ...; or (c) ... is required, or expressly permitted, by a law" ((d), (e) likewise).
-- s 27(1): a contract alleged to be standard form "is presumed to be a standard form contract unless another party ... proves
-- otherwise".
-- s 23(1): "A term of a consumer contract or small business contract is void if: (a) the term is unfair; and (b) the contract
-- is a standard form contract." (2A): a person contravenes if it makes such a contract and "proposed the unfair term"; (2B): "a
-- separate contravention ... in respect of each term".
DECLARE `Contested term` HAS
    `would cause a significant imbalance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the advantaged party proves it reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would cause detriment if relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defines the main subject matter, sets the upfront price or is required or permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party proves the contract is not standard form` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is this term unfair (Sch 2 s 24)?
GIVEN `the clause` IS A `Contested term` @desc The term, and what it does to the balance between the parties
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the term unfair` IF
        `the clause`'s `would cause a significant imbalance`
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `the advantaged party proves it reasonably necessary`)
    AND `the clause`'s `would cause detriment if relied on`

@export Is this term of my standard form contract void as unfair (Sch 2 ss 23(1), 26, 27)?
GIVEN `the clause` IS A `Contested term` @desc The term, and the facts that bear on whether it is unfair
      `it is a consumer or small business contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is a consumer contract or a small business contract (s 23(3), (4))
      `it is a financial product or for financial services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is a financial product or for financial services (then the ASIC Act applies instead, s 131A(2)(b))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the term void as unfair` IF
        `it is a consumer or small business contract`
    AND (NOT `it is a financial product or for financial services`)
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `defines the main subject matter, sets the upfront price or is required or permitted by law`)
    AND `Is the term unfair` `the clause`
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `the other party proves the contract is not standard form`)

@export Would I contravene the Act by proposing this term in my standard form contract (Sch 2 s 23(2A), (2B))?
GIVEN `the clause` IS A `Contested term` @desc The term you propose, and the facts that bear on whether it is unfair
      `it is a consumer or small business contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is a consumer contract or a small business contract
      `I proposed the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, not the other party, put the term forward
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would proposing the term contravene s 23(2A)` IF
    `Is the term void as unfair` `the clause` `it is a consumer or small business contract` FALSE AND `I proposed the term`

§§ `Sch 2 ss 69, 73, 75 -- the door-knock and the cold call`

-- s 69(1): "An agreement is an unsolicited consumer agreement if: (a) it is for the supply, in trade or commerce, of goods or
-- services to a consumer; and (b) it is made as a result of negotiations between a dealer and the consumer: (i) in each
-- other's presence at a place other than the business or trade premises of the supplier ...; or (ii) by telephone; ... and (c)
-- the consumer did not invite the dealer to come to that place, or to make a telephone call, for the purposes of entering into
-- negotiations relating to the supply of those goods or services ...; and (d) the total price ...: (i) is not ascertainable at
-- the time the agreement is made; or (ii) if it is ascertainable at that time--is more than $100 or such other amount
-- prescribed". No other amount is prescribed in the deposited Regulations. (2): "An invitation merely to quote a price for a
-- supply is not taken ... to be an invitation". (4), reg 81: not an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is "(a) a business
-- contract; (b) a discontinued negotiations agreement; (c) an agreement made in the course of a party plan event; (d) a
-- renewable agreement of the same kind; (e) a subsequent agreement of the same kind" -- one input.
DECLARE `My agreement` HAS
    `for the supply of goods or services to me as a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `negotiated face to face away from the supplier's premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `negotiated by telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I invited the dealer to negotiate that supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total price was ascertainable when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `total price` IS A NUMBER
    `of a kind reg 81 excludes` IS A BOOLEAN

`the s 69 price floor` MEANS 100

@export Is my agreement an unsolicited consumer agreement (Sch 2 s 69; reg 81)?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My agreement` @desc How the agreement came about and its price
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an unsolicited consumer agreement` IF
        `the agreement`'s `for the supply of goods or services to me as a consumer`
    AND (`the agreement`'s `negotiated face to face away from the supplier's premises` OR `the agreement`'s `negotiated by telephone`)
    AND (NOT `the agreement`'s `I invited the dealer to negotiate that supply`)
    AND ((NOT `the agreement`'s `the total price was ascertainable when it was made`) OR `the agreement`'s `total price` GREATER THAN `the s 69 price floor`)
    AND (NOT `the agreement`'s `of a kind reg 81 excludes`)

-- s 73(1): "A dealer must not call on a person for the purpose of negotiating an unsolicited consumer agreement ...: (a) at any
-- time on a Sunday or a public holiday; or (b) before 9 am on any other day; or (c) after 6 pm on any other day (or after 5 pm
-- if the other day is a Saturday)." (2): not if the dealer calls "in accordance with consent that ... was not given in the
-- presence of the dealer". "Call on" does not include a telephone call (s 2).
DECLARE `Kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `a Sunday or public holiday`
    `a Saturday`
    `a weekday that is not a public holiday`

@export May a door-to-door dealer call on me at this time (Sch 2 s 73)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A `Kind of day` @desc The kind of day the dealer calls
      `the time` IS A NUMBER @desc The time the dealer calls, as hhmm on a 24-hour clock (5.30 pm is 1730)
      `I consented other than in the dealer's presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed to this visit beforehand, not face to face with the dealer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the dealer call on me now` IF
    `I consented other than in the dealer's presence`
    OR (CONSIDER `the day`
        WHEN `a Sunday or public holiday` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a Saturday` THEN `the time` AT LEAST 900 AND `the time` AT MOST 1700
        WHEN `a weekday that is not a public holiday` THEN `the time` AT LEAST 900 AND `the time` AT MOST 1800)

-- s 75(1): the dealer "must leave the premises immediately on the request of" the occupier or the prospective consumer. (2):
-- the dealer "must not contact the prospective consumer for the purpose of negotiating an unsolicited consumer agreement ... for
-- at least 30 days after the prospective consumer makes the request". Read: contact is barred on each of the 30 days after the
-- request.
`the s 75 quiet period in days` MEANS 30

@export After I asked the dealer to leave, may they contact me again to negotiate (Sch 2 s 75(2))?
GIVEN `days since I asked them to leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since you asked the dealer to leave
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the dealer contact me again` IF
    `days since I asked them to leave` GREATER THAN `the s 75 quiet period in days`

§§ `Sch 2 ss 82, 85(3), 86; reg 95 -- the termination period`

-- s 82(1): the consumer "may, during the period provided under subsection (3), terminate the agreement by indicating, in an
-- oral or written notice to the supplier ..., an intention to terminate"; (2): "despite affirmation" and "even though the
-- agreement has been fully executed". (3): the period is "whichever of the following periods is the longest": (a), (b) to "the
-- end of the tenth business day after" the day the agreement was made (in person) or the day the agreement document was given
-- (telephone); (c) "3 months" if s 73, 74 or 75 was contravened; (d) "6 months" if s 76, a provision of Subdivision C (ss
-- 78-81) or s 86 was contravened; (e) "such other period as the agreement provides" (not modelled). s 2: a business day is
-- not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday where the agreement was made. The count of business days is an input.
DECLARE `My termination period` IS ONE OF
    `ten business days`
    `three months`
    `six months`

@export How long do I have to cancel my unsolicited consumer agreement (Sch 2 s 82(3))?
GIVEN `the dealer broke the hours, disclosure or leave-on-request rules (ss 73-75)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dealer called outside permitted hours, did not say who they were and why they came, or did not leave when asked
      `the dealer or supplier broke the information, document or no-supply rules (ss 76, 78-81, 86)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not told of your right to cancel, the agreement document was defective, or you were supplied or charged within the first ten business days
GIVETH A `My termination period`
DECIDE `How long do I have to cancel` IS
    IF `the dealer or supplier broke the information, document or no-supply rules (ss 76, 78-81, 86)`
    THEN `six months`
    ELSE IF `the dealer broke the hours, disclosure or leave-on-request rules (ss 73-75)`
         THEN `three months`
         ELSE `ten business days`

`the cooling-off business days` MEANS 10

@export May I still cancel my unsolicited consumer agreement (Sch 2 s 82)?
GIVEN `my period` IS A `My termination period` @desc Which termination period applies to you
      `business days since the start day` IS A NUMBER @desc Business days since the agreement was made (or, after a phone sale, since you were given the agreement document)
      `still within that many months starting the day after the start day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a three- or six-month period: whether that many months, counted from the day after the start day, have not yet ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still cancel` IF
    CONSIDER `my period`
    WHEN `ten business days` THEN `business days since the start day` AT MOST `the cooling-off business days`
    OTHERWISE `business days since the start day` AT MOST `the cooling-off business days` OR `still within that many months starting the day after the start day`

-- s 86(1): the supplier "must not: (a) supply to the consumer ... the goods or services ...; or (b) accept any payment ...; or
-- (c) require any payment ...; during" the period to the end of the tenth business day. Reg 95: s 86(1)(a) "does not apply to
-- the supply of goods ... if the total price payable for the goods under the agreement is $500 or less" (goods only).
`the reg 95 goods price` MEANS 500

@export May the supplier take or ask for payment from me yet (Sch 2 s 86(1)(b), (c))?
GIVEN `business days since the start day` IS A NUMBER @desc Business days since the agreement was made (or, after a phone sale, since you were given the agreement document)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the supplier take payment yet` IF
    `business days since the start day` GREATER THAN `the cooling-off business days`

@export May the supplier deliver the goods or start the services yet (Sch 2 s 86(1)(a); reg 95)?
GIVEN `business days since the start day` IS A NUMBER @desc Business days since the agreement was made (or, after a phone sale, since you were given the agreement document)
      `goods rather than services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is for goods (reg 95 covers goods only)
      `total price of the goods` IS A NUMBER @desc The total price payable for the goods under the agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the supplier supply me yet` IF
        `business days since the start day` GREATER THAN `the cooling-off business days`
    OR  (`goods rather than services` AND `total price of the goods` AT MOST `the reg 95 goods price`)

-- s 85(3): if the agreement is terminated after the tenth business day, the goods come back and "the consumer has failed to
-- take reasonable care of the goods; the consumer is liable to pay compensation ... for the damage to, or depreciation in the
-- value of, the goods". (5): "not liable for any such damage or depreciation attributable to normal use of the goods or to
-- circumstances beyond the consumer's control".
@export Having cancelled, must I pay the supplier for damage to the goods (Sch 2 s 85(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `I cancelled after the tenth business day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cancelled after the first ten business days
      `I failed to take reasonable care of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to take reasonable care of the goods
      `the damage came only from normal use or things beyond my control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the damage or loss of value came only from normal use or circumstances beyond your control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I compensate the supplier for the goods` IF
        `I cancelled after the tenth business day`
    AND `I failed to take reasonable care of the goods`
    AND (NOT `the damage came only from normal use or things beyond my control`)

§§ `Sch 2 s 18 -- misleading or deceptive conduct`

-- s 18(1): "A person must not, in trade or commerce, engage in conduct that is misleading or deceptive or is likely to mislead
-- or deceive." Whether a name is likely to mislead is a judgment, asked as a fact. s 131A(2)(a): Part 2-1 does not apply as
-- Commonwealth law "to conduct engaged in in relation to financial services".
@export Is the other trader's conduct a contravention of s 18 (Sch 2 s 18; s 131A(2)(a))?
GIVEN `they are a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other trader is a corporation
      `in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is in trade or commerce (any business or professional activity)
      `misleading or deceptive or likely to mislead or deceive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is misleading or deceptive, or likely to be (a judgment for a court)
      `in relation to financial services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is in relation to financial services
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does their conduct contravene s 18` IF
        `Does the ACL reach my dealing as Commonwealth law` `they are a corporation` `in relation to financial services`
    AND `in trade or commerce`
    AND `misleading or deceptive or likely to mislead or deceive`

§§ `Sch 2 s 50 -- what a collector may not do`

-- s 50(1): "A person must not use physical force, or undue harassment or coercion, in connection with: (a) the supply or
-- possible supply of goods or services; or (b) the payment for goods or services; or (c) the sale or grant ... of an interest
-- in land; or (d) the payment for an interest in land." s 131A(1): the Division applying the Schedule as Commonwealth law
-- "does not apply ... to the supply ... of services that are financial services, or of financial products". A credit card
-- debt is a financial product (an inference; the ASIC Act is not deposited), so its collection is not reached here.
DECLARE `What s 50 says about it` IS ONE OF
    `s 50 forbids it`
    `s 50 does not forbid it`
    `s 50 does not reach it as Commonwealth law: the debt is for financial services or products`

@export May the debt collector do this to me (Sch 2 s 50; s 131A)?
GIVEN `the collector is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the collector (or the creditor it acts for) is a corporation
      `the debt is for financial services or a financial product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the debt is for credit, a loan, a credit card or another financial product
      `connected with payment for goods, services or land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the demand is about paying for goods, services or land
      `physical force, undue harassment or coercion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the collector used physical force, or undue harassment or coercion (a judgment for a court)
GIVETH A `What s 50 says about it`
DECIDE `What does s 50 say about the collector` IS
    IF (NOT `Does the ACL reach my dealing as Commonwealth law` `the collector is a corporation` `the debt is for financial services or a financial product`)
    THEN `s 50 does not reach it as Commonwealth law: the debt is for financial services or products`
    ELSE IF `connected with payment for goods, services or land` AND `physical force, undue harassment or coercion`
         THEN `s 50 forbids it`
         ELSE `s 50 does not forbid it`

§§ `Part IVA -- must I notify the ACCC of my acquisition`

-- s 51ABB(1): the acquisitions provisions apply to "(a) an acquisition by a corporation of shares in the capital of a body
-- corporate; (b) an acquisition by a corporation of any assets of a person" and acquisitions of shares in or assets of a
-- corporation. s 51ABD(1): not to "a restructure or reorganisation of a group of persons who are related" bodies corporate.
-- s 51ABO: an acquisition "is required to be notified if: (a) the acquisition is put into effect on or after 1 January 2026;
-- and (b) the acquisition: (i) occurs in circumstances determined under subsection 51ABP(1) ...; or (ii) is in a class of
-- acquisitions determined under subsection 51ABQ(1) ...; and (c)" is not in circumstances or a class exempted under ss 51ABRA,
-- 51ABRB. s 51ABP(1), (2): "The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine circumstances" which "must be determined
-- wholly or partly by reference to the acquisition meeting a specified threshold". THE THRESHOLDS ARE IN THE MINISTER'S
-- DETERMINATION, NOT IN THE ACT, AND IT IS NOT DEPOSITED: whether one is met is an INPUT.
-- s 51ABS(1): a share acquisition "is not required to be notified if: (a) immediately after ... the person does not control
-- ... the body corporate; or (b) the person controlled the body corporate immediately before", unless (5) it is in a class the
-- Minister determines under (6). s 51ABT(1): shares in a Chapter 6 entity need no notice unless someone's voting power rises
-- "from 20% or below to more than 20%" or "from a starting point that is above 20% and below 100%". s 51ABJ(1): a Chapter 6
-- entity is "(a) a listed company ...; or (b) an unlisted company with more than 50 members ...; or (c) a listed registered
-- scheme". s 51ABV(1): the ACCC may determine on a waiver application "that the acquisition is not required to be notified".
-- s 51ABE(1), (2): an acquisition that "is required to be notified; but ... is not a notified acquisition" "is stayed".
@export Is the company I am acquiring a Chapter 6 entity (s 51ABJ)?
GIVEN `listed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is listed on a stock exchange
      `members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members (shareholders) the company has, joint holders counted once
      `a listed registered scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a listed registered managed investment scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the target a Chapter 6 entity` IF
    `listed` OR `members` GREATER THAN 50 OR `a listed registered scheme`

DECLARE `My acquisition of a business` HAS
    `the acquisitions provisions apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an internal restructure of related bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `put into effect on` IS A NUMBER
    `meets a threshold the Minister has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a class the Minister has determined notifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in circumstances or a class the Minister has exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I control the target afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I controlled the target before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a class the Minister determined under s 51ABS(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the target is a Chapter 6 entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `someone's voting power crosses 20 per cent or rises from above it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ACCC has granted a waiver` IS A BOOLEAN

`the start of mandatory notification` MEANS 20260101

@export Must I notify the ACCC of my acquisition (Part IVA ss 51ABB, 51ABD, 51ABO, 51ABP, 51ABS, 51ABT, 51ABV)?
GIVEN `the deal` IS A `My acquisition of a business` @desc The acquisition: what is acquired, when, whether a threshold or class is met, and control before and after
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the ACCC` IF
        `the deal`'s `the acquisitions provisions apply to it`
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `an internal restructure of related bodies corporate`)
    AND `the deal`'s `put into effect on` AT LEAST `the start of mandatory notification`
    AND (`the deal`'s `meets a threshold the Minister has determined` OR `the deal`'s `in a class the Minister has determined notifiable`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `in circumstances or a class the Minister has exempted`)
    AND (NOT (    `the deal`'s `of shares`
              AND ((NOT `the deal`'s `I control the target afterwards`) OR `the deal`'s `I controlled the target before`)
              AND (NOT `the deal`'s `in a class the Minister determined under s 51ABS(6)`)))
    AND (NOT (`the deal`'s `of shares` AND `the deal`'s `the target is a Chapter 6 entity` AND (NOT `the deal`'s `someone's voting power crosses 20 per cent or rises from above it`)))
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `the ACCC has granted a waiver`)

@export Is my acquisition stayed because I have not notified it (s 51ABE(2))?
GIVEN `the deal` IS A `My acquisition of a business` @desc The acquisition
      `I have notified it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the ACCC of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my acquisition stayed for want of notice` IF
    `Must I notify the ACCC` `the deal` AND (NOT `I have notified it`)
